* @title Gimpel MFREAD multi-file interleaved reading
* @attribution James F. Gimpel, Algorithms in SNOBOL4, Chapter 9.6 (MFREAD)
* @expect >>>
* A:apple
* B:banana
* A:apricot
* B:blueberry
* A:avocado
* B:blackberry
* B:boysenberry
* A-again:apple
* <<<
-INCLUDE "MFREAD.INC"
*  Interleave reads from two named data files. MFREAD associates each
*  unit number with its filename on the first call and keeps a separate
*  buffer + EOF counter per unit, so reads from A and B do not collide.
LOOP	X = MFREAD(, 8, 'MFA.IN')       :F(B_TURN)
	OUTPUT = 'A:' X
B_TURN	Y = MFREAD(, 9, 'MFB.IN')       :F(REW)
	OUTPUT = 'B:' Y                 :(LOOP)
*  REWIND clears the per-unit state so the next MFREAD on that unit
*  re-opens the file from the top, demonstrated by re-reading A's
*  first line after both streams have been exhausted.
REW	REWIND(8)
	X = MFREAD(, 8, 'MFA.IN')       :F(DONE)
	OUTPUT = 'A-again:' X
DONE
END
